.TH VIBEMDM-AGENT 8 "October 2026" "VibeMDM" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
vibemdm-agent \- VibeMDM management agent for macOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vibemdm-agent
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B vibemdm-agent help
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vibemdm-agent
connects a Mac to a VibeMDM server. It runs scripts and policies, installs
packages and apps (through Installomator), collects inventory, enforces
restricted software, ships logs, hosts the local Self Service portal, runs
compliance scans and onboarding workflows, and provides the audited remote
shell. It complements, and does not replace, the MDM enrollment profile.
.PP
The daemon runs as root under launchd (label
.BR com.vibemdm.agent )
and keeps a long-poll connection to the server so console actions take effect
within about a second.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B enroll \-\-server \fIURL\fP [\-\-token \fITOKEN\fP] [\-\-mdm] [\-\-allow\-insecure\-http]
Enroll this Mac and install the launchd services. The token may instead be
given in the
.B VIBEMDM_ENROLL_TOKEN
environment variable (recommended: arguments are visible in
.BR ps (1)).
.B \-\-mdm
also saves the MDM enrollment profile to /Users/Shared and opens it.
The server URL must use https unless
.B \-\-allow\-insecure\-http
is given. Requires root.
.TP
.B status
Show enrollment, server reachability and local component status.
.TP
.B policy \fR[\fB\-\-event\fP \fINAME\fP]
Check in and run policies for a trigger (default
.BR checkin ).
Requires root.
.TP
.B trigger \fIevent\fP
Ask the running daemon to fire a trigger. Unprivileged users may fire only
.BR login ,
.B checkin
and
.BR network_change .
.TP
.B recon
Collect and submit inventory. Requires root.
.TP
.B checkin
Run one check-in cycle. Requires root.
.TP
.B check\-connection
Verify the server is reachable with this Mac's credentials.
.TP
.B selfservice
Open the Self Service portal (http://127.0.0.1:8571).
.TP
.B manage
Reinstall the launchd daemon and login agent. Requires root.
.TP
.B remove\-framework
Unenroll and remove the agent. Requires root.
.TP
.B daemon
Run the agent daemon (started by launchd).
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/vibemdm\-agent
The agent binary.
.TP
.I /Library/Application Support/VibeMDM/agent.json
Server URL and device credentials (mode 0600).
.TP
.I /Library/Application Support/VibeMDM/disable\-remote\-shell
If present and owned by root, the Mac refuses remote shell sessions.
.TP
.I /var/run/vibemdm\-agent.sock
Trigger socket for built-in triggers (any user).
.TP
.I /var/run/vibemdm\-agent.sock.root
Trigger socket for any trigger (root only).
.TP
.I /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.vibemdm.agent.plist
launchd job for the daemon.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error, 2 on a usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo VIBEMDM_ENROLL_TOKEN=xxxx vibemdm\-agent enroll \-\-server https://mdm.example.com \-\-mdm
sudo vibemdm\-agent policy \-\-event install_zoom
vibemdm\-agent status
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vibemdm (8),
.BR launchctl (1),
.BR profiles (1)
.PP
The VibeMDM administrator manual, docs/manual/ in the source tree.
